<p class="lead-paragraph">Gerund or infinitive after a verb? This single choice quietly costs SSC CGL and Bank PO aspirants more marks than almost any other grammar point. Not because the forms are difficult, but because textbooks give long memorisation lists instead of the clear patterns that examiners actually test. Once you see the system behind the lists, the confusion disappears.</p>

<div style="background:#f0f7ff;border-left:4px solid #1B3A6B;padding:15px 18px;margin:20px 0;border-radius:4px;">
<p style="margin:0;"><strong>Quick Answer:</strong> After certain verbs we use only the gerund (-ing), after others only the infinitive (to + verb), and after a small group both forms are possible but the meaning changes. Mastering these three groups is enough for almost every exam question.</p>
</div>

